g=5 mg/L), this yields a ~3.27e-4 discrepancy against a 1e-9 tolerance — a deterministic failure. The correct fix is to update the test constants to match the implementation's molar-mass-derived values, which are scientifically more precise. This is a real broken test that should be fixed regardless of whether it was introduced by recent changes."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7ca6f750-b291-4f72-b520-ac575b925b69"}
